# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 6 — G7: the CALL-SITE-SCOPED shape, which no artifact in this
# tree had ever expressed.
#
# ⛔⛔ WHY THIS RUNG WAS MISSING, AND WHY THAT MATTERED. Slice 4 proved two things and left the
# combination unbuilt:
#
#   G3  the two guard positions close all six starvation shapes   — but the guard is on the SHARED rule
#   G4  a residual-FREE holder of that shared rule then BREAKS    — `k = n;` REJECTs
#   G5  removing the trailing guard un-breaks it                  — so G4's REJECT is the guard, not the shape
#
# ⇒ the decision was *"the guard is call-site scoped, so it lands on a clone reached only from the
# holder"* — a shape with G3's power and without G4's damage. Nothing measured it. This file is that
# shape, and it is the rule-for-rule TARGET the planner must synthesize (`.17` slice 7).
#
# THE ONE-DIFFERENCE PAIR IS G4 ↔ G7. Identical holders, identical inputs; the only change is WHERE
# the two lookaheads live:
#
#   G4   outer_cast := ct …                 ct := kw | prim     prim := … &( … )   ← on the shared rule
#   G7   outer_cast := ct_guard …           ct := kw | prim     prim := …          ← untouched
#                                           ct_guard := kw | prim_guard
#                                                               prim_guard := … &( … )
#
# THE CLONE CHAIN, and its length is exactly the census's `guard_hops`. The holder does not name the
# base rule — it names `ct`, which is TRANSPARENT to `prim` — so pushing one lookahead down to the
# `*` costs one guarded clone per transparent hop plus the guarded base itself. Here `guard_hops = 1`
# ⇒ `ct_guard` + `prim_guard`.
#
# ⭐ THE FALLBACK IS THE WHOLE MECHANISM, and it is why the guard must sit INSIDE a choice rather
# than at the holder's own call. On `k = t'(n);` the seed `cast_seed` matches `t'(n)` entire, the
# trailing guard refuses it, and `prim_guard` FAILS — at which point `ct_guard`'s other alternative
# `kw` wins with the short match `t`, and `outer_cast` gets its `'(n)` back. A guard that made
# `outer_cast` itself fail would have nothing to fall back to.
#
# ⛔ WHAT THIS FILE MUST DO: accept e1–e6 (the guarded chain closes every starvation G3 closed) AND
# e7 (`k = n;`, the residual-free holder, which G4 REJECTS). A single grammar doing both is the
# design's whole claim. If e7 ever REJECTs here, the clone chain is not actually isolating the two
# call sites and `.17`'s decision is wrong.
#
# The entry rule is named `scratch` so this file loads into the scratch slot verbatim:
#   cp <this file> grammars/scratch/scratch.ebnf && make -C rust SHELL=/bin/bash focus_scratch
@entry: true
scratch := kw_k eq outer_cast semi
         | kw_k eq prim semi

# ---- the residual-BEARING holder, redirected to the guarded chain. This is the only edit a
# transformation would make to an existing rule: the left corner is repointed, every other element
# (and therefore every `$N` position in its annotation) is preserved.
outer_cast := ct_guard tick lparen lit rparen

# ---- the ORIGINALS, untouched. `scratch`'s second alternative reaches `prim` through them and must
# keep the unguarded behaviour — that is the whole point of cloning instead of editing in place.
ct := kw | prim
prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix )*

# ---- the GUARDED CLONE CHAIN, reachable only from `outer_cast`.
# `ct_guard` is `ct` with its transparent arm repointed; its OTHER alternative is copied verbatim,
# and that copy is what the tournament falls back to when the guard refuses the seed.
ct_guard := kw | prim_guard
prim_guard := prim_base ( prim_suffix &( tick lparen lit rparen ) )* &( tick lparen lit rparen )

# ---- shared by both chains: the seed set and the iterated suffix are NOT cloned, because neither
# carries a guard. Only the rules on the path from the holder down to the `*` are.
prim_base := lit | cast_seed
cast_seed := kw tick lparen lit rparen
prim_suffix := tick lparen lit rparen

# ---- the token tier. Every token begins with `trivia`, exactly as `grammars/systemverilog.ebnf`
# writes `tick := trivia "'"` (:7151), `lparen := trivia "("` (:7105), `rparen := trivia ")"` (:7130).
lit := trivia /n/
kw := trivia /t/
kw_k := trivia /k/
eq := trivia "="
semi := trivia ";"
tick := trivia "'"
lparen := trivia "("
rparen := trivia ")"

# ---- the layout tier, copied in shape from `grammars/systemverilog.ebnf:618-624`. NULLABLE, and it
# leads every token — which is precisely why `/` is in the FIRST set of every token and why a
# byte-set guard over FIRST(residual) cannot be exact anywhere on SystemVerilog.
@branch_policy: priority_first
trivia := (line_comment | block_comment)*
line_comment := /\/\/[^\n]*(\n|$)/
block_comment := /\/\*([^*]|\*+[^*\/])*\*+\//
